  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "@imcp-pro/dsh-client-background",
      "text": "English | [中文](README.zh.md)\n\n[](LICENSE)\n\nA [dsh](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness) Web client bundle that replaces the base background with a randomly rotating [Unsplash](https://unsplash.com) wallpaper, revealed through translucent surfaces."
    },
    {
      "section": "Features",
      "text": "- **100 curated wallpapers** rotate on a configurable interval.\n- **Runtime switch** — disable the effect without uninstalling the plugin.\n- **Client-side update check** — polls GitHub for a newer commit and surfaces the exact update command.\n- **No framework coupling** — the visual effect uses only browser globals (`document`, `Image`, `setInterval`)."
    },
    {
      "section": "Requirements",
      "text": "- A dsh `web` profile (`dsh --profile web`, a.k.a. `dsh web`) with the `web-app` bundle.\n- A dsh build that exposes the base theme tokens `--dsw-alias-bg-base` / `--dsw-specific-sidebar-fill`, toggles the `body[data-ds-dark-theme]` dark-mode attribute, and serves the Plugins settings panel."
    },
    {
      "section": "Themes",
      "text": "The effect adapts to the active dsh theme — translucent white surfaces in light mode, translucent dark surfaces in dark mode — so it follows your theme (and system) automatically. **Dark mode is recommended**: the photo reads as a moody, high-contrast backdrop. In light mode the photo shows through a white veil with a slight darkening and looks more subdued."
    },
    {
      "section": "From GitHub",
      "text": "```sh\ndsh plugin --profile web add github:imcp-pro/dsh-client-background\n```\n\nThe plugin's `prepare` script builds `lib/` at install time (it is not committed), and pnpm ≥ 10 blocks a git dependency's build scripts until allowlisted. The first run may therefore fail with `ERR_PNPM_GIT_DEP_PREPARE_NOT_ALLOWED` — that is expected. To resolve it:"
    },
    {
      "section": "From GitHub",
      "text": "1. Copy the exact allowlist key printed under **\"For example\"** in the error:\n   `@imcp-pro/dsh-client-background@https://codeload.github.com/…/tar.gz/<commit>`.\n2. Paste it under `allowBuilds` in the web profile's `pnpm-workspace.yaml`\n   (`~/.dsh/profiles/web/pnpm-workspace.yaml`), then re-run the command.\n\n```yaml"
    },
    {
      "section": "~/.dsh/profiles/web/pnpm-workspace.yaml",
      "text": "allowBuilds:\n  \"@imcp-pro/dsh-client-background@https://codeload.github.com/imcp-pro/dsh-client-background/tar.gz/<commit>\": true\n```\n\n> **Note:** the key is commit-bound — every new commit changes `<commit>`, so always copy the key from the current error. Keep the codeload tarball form (`https://codeload.github.com/…/tar.gz/<commit>`) verbatim, not `git+https://` or `git+ssh://`."
    },
    {
      "section": "From an agent (dsh / Claude Code / OpenCode)",
      "text": "Paste the following prompt into your agent; it installs the plugin and resolves the allowlist step for you:\n\n```text\nInstall the dsh background plugin for the web profile:\n\ndsh plugin --profile web add github:imcp-pro/dsh-client-background"
    },
    {
      "section": "From a local checkout",
      "text": "```sh\nnpm run build\ndsh plugin --profile web add .\n```\n\nThen restart `dsh web`; the background appears and persists across restarts."
    },
    {
      "section": "Configuration",
      "text": "Open **Settings → Plugins → Plugin list**, then expand **Wallpaper background** under **Global plugins**:\n\n| Field | Default | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Enable background | on | runtime off switch; the plugin stays installed |\n| Rotation interval (seconds) | 20 | how often the image auto-switches |\n| Check for updates | off | periodically poll GitHub for a newer commit |\n| Check interval (seconds) | 21600 | time between two update checks |"
    },
    {
      "section": "Configuration",
      "text": "Edits stage locally and apply on **Save**; **Discard** drops them. When a newer commit is found, the entry shows the update command to run (then restart)."
    },
    {
      "section": "Development",
      "text": "```sh\nnpm install\nnpm run build   # esbuild bundles + tsc declarations → lib/\nnpm test        # vitest (jsdom)\n```\n\n`tsconfig.json` maps the `@deepseek-ai/dsh-*` type imports to a sibling deepseek-harness source checkout (its `lib/types`), because the published dsh packages currently predate the source API this plugin targets. Point the `paths` entries at your own checkout before building."
    },
    {
      "section": "Publishing",
      "text": "```sh\nnpm publish    # `prepare` runs the build; ships lib/ + cordis.patch.yml\n```\n\nThe package ships `lib/` and `cordis.patch.yml`. It declares `dsh.bundle.patch` (so `dsh plugin add` registers the layer), `dsh.client` (so the client-modules host serves the browser half), and a `client-background` settings namespace the Host half registers."
    },
    {
      "section": "Notes",
      "text": "- **Instant swap, not crossfade** — preloading removes the loading flash, but the image still changes in one step.\n- **`background-attachment: fixed` is ignored on iOS Safari** — the image scrolls with the page there.\n- **The update check is client-side** — the browser polls the GitHub default branch and compares its commit with the one stamped into the bundle at build time, so it never mutates a running install."
    },
    {
      "section": "License",
      "text": "[MIT](LICENSE)"
    }
